    {
      "paragraph": 265,
      "text": "Figure S3: 31P-NMR of prolonged incubation samples demonstrates GTP dephosphorylation. Overnight incubation of enzymes with GTP does show that GTP is dephosphorylated by HFP and IMP after prolonged incubation at 55\u02da C.  In particular, note the formation of the peak at 2.1 ppm which is free phosphate (highlighted by the gray box). A free phosphate peak is absent in the GTP standard, which was subjected to identical temperature and duration of incubation. ",
